From: FlipperOneEmu
Subject: [PATCH] hw/ufs: answer DME_RESET and DME_ENABLE

A UFS host's driver may reset and enable the UniPro stack (UIC commands
DME_RESET and DME_ENABLE) before it sets its PHY up and starts the link:
Linux's driver for Rockchip's RK3576 host does, as the host is enabled.
QEMU's UFS answers both FAILURE, so the host never comes up. The emulated
link has no PHY to reset or enable: answer SUCCESS, as for DME_SET.

---
--- a/hw/ufs/ufs.c
+++ b/hw/ufs/ufs.c
@@ -418,6 +418,15 @@
             u->reg.hcs = FIELD_DP32(u->reg.hcs, HCS, UPMCRS, UFS_PWR_LOCAL);
         }
         break;
+    case UFS_UIC_CMD_DME_RESET:
+    case UFS_UIC_CMD_DME_ENABLE:
+        /*
+         * The emulated link has no PHY to reset or to enable. Some hosts'
+         * drivers (Rockchip's) reset and enable the UniPro stack before
+         * they configure their PHY and start the link.
+         */
+        u->reg.ucmdarg2 = UFS_UIC_CMD_RESULT_SUCCESS;
+        break;
     /*
      * TODO: Revisit after PM implementation
      * Power Management is not supported in current QEMU-UFS,
